{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And covered the chariots, all Pharaoh's host.</b> Thus is the way of Scriptures to write an extra lamed — as in ״לְכָל כֵּלָיו תַּעֲשֶׂה נְחֹשֶׁת״ (Exodus 27), and likewise ״לְכֹל כְּלֵי הַמִּשְׁכָּן בְּכֹל עֲבֹדָתוֹ״ (Numbers 4), ״וִיתֵדוֹתָם וּמֵיתְרֵיהֶם לְכָל כְּלֵיהֶם״ (there) — and it is nothing but a grammatical refinement."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:14.440578208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}